hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24301","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh narrated to us, from Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Ahjar al-Zayt praying for rain, raising the insides of his palms."
"24302","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh narrated to us, from Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, who said: I used to graze at Dhat al-Jaysh, and I was struck by need, so I mentioned that to some of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they directed me to a garden of one of the Ansar, so I cut some clusters from it, and they seized me and took me to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I told him of my need, so he gave me one cluster and returned the rest to its owners."
"24303","Safwan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, from Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, who said: My master ordered me to dry meat for him, and a poor man came and I fed him from it, and he learned of me and beat me, so I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him, and he said: Why did you beat him, he said: He gave my food without my order, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The reward is between you both."
